UFT PHOENIX SOFTWARE LICENSE AGREEMENT

PROPRIETARY SOFTWARE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

IMPORTANT — READ CAREFULLY. This Software License Agreement (the
"Agreement") is a legal agreement between the licensee ("Customer", "you")
and Merito Solutions, Inc. ("Merito", "Licensor") governing the use of the
UFT Phoenix software, including its command-line tools, graphical
interface, converters, documentation, and any updates provided to you
(collectively, the "Software"). If you accept this Agreement for a company
or other organization, including by deploying the Software in a silent
installation with the installer's /ACCEPTEULA option, you accept it on
that organization's behalf and confirm that you have authority to bind it,
and "you" means that organization. If you do not have that authority, you
accept this Agreement for yourself, and you may not install or use the
Software for that organization. The Software has a Free Edition and a
Licensed Edition, described in section 1.

BY INSTALLING, COPYING, OR OTHERWISE USING THE SOFTWARE, YOU AGREE TO BE
BOUND BY THE TERMS OF THIS AGREEMENT. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE, DO NOT INSTALL
OR USE THE SOFTWARE.

1. DEFINITIONS AND LICENSE GRANT
   a. Definitions. In this Agreement:
      "ALM" means OpenText Application Quality Management (formerly
      ALM/Quality Center), the test management server the Software works
      with. An "ALM project" is one project in one domain on one ALM
      server.
      "Test Case" means a UFT One GUI test. In an ALM project, a Test Case
      is a test of type QUICKTEST_TEST, including an API test that ALM
      stores under that type; tests of other types are not Test Cases. On a
      file system, a Test Case is a folder that holds both a Test.tsp file
      and a .usr file. A test is a Test Case whether or not the Software
      can analyze or convert it, and whether or not it has already been
      converted to Python. Function libraries, object repositories,
      actions, and other resources are not Test Cases.
      "Conversion" means the set of Test Cases that one run of the
      Software covers: every Test Case in one ALM project, including any
      in ALM's Unattached area, or under all the source folders of one
      file-system run, counted before any test is parked, excluded, or
      filtered out of the run. Tests inside a folder named Recycle Bin or
      .TrashCan, at any level within the ALM project or below the run's
      source folders, are not counted. Tests inside a folder named out,
      .git, or __pycache__ below the run's source folders are not counted
      unless the run converts them. A copy of a Test Case that the
      Software itself made, such as a backup or a converted copy in its
      output folder, is not counted. A Conversion is that set of Test
      Cases, not the act of converting them.
      To "convert" a Test Case means to use the Software to produce a
      converted version of it, as the Software does in Step 6 (Review and
      Run) of its Migration Console and in the equivalent commands,
      whether the Software builds that version only, saves or uploads it,
      or rehearses saving or uploading it.
      "Assessment" means using the Software to discover, analyze,
      measure, and report on Test Cases, as the Software does in Step 5
      (Analysis and Reports) of its Migration Console and in the
      equivalent commands, including an analysis that builds tests only
      to measure them; building a test only to measure it is not
      converting it. "Assessment Output" means the reports, the scoping
      summary, the report the Software titles "Technical Conversion
      Breakdown", and any test that an Assessment produces.
      "Converted Assets" means the converted tests and other assets that
      the Software produces from your source assets when you convert Test
      Cases as this Agreement permits.
      "Deploy" means to save or upload a converted test to ALM or to any
      other place where you keep tests for use, or to use it in your
      regular testing.
      "Order" means an order form, statement of work, or other written
      agreement for the Software signed by you and Merito.
      "License File" means a file that Merito issues to you under an
      Order and signs digitally. It names you as the licensee and states
      the largest Conversion, in Test Cases, that it covers (or that it
      has no limit), its expiry date (or that it does not expire), and
      any ALM projects to which it is limited.
      A capitalized word has the meaning this section 1.a gives it; the
      same word in lower case, and any product feature name, has its
      ordinary meaning.
   b. Free Edition. Subject to the terms of this Agreement, Merito grants
      you, free of charge, a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
      non-sublicensable license to install and use the Software, in
      object and script form, solely for your internal business purpose
      of assessing and migrating your own OpenText UFT One / Micro Focus
      UFT test assets (the "Free Edition"). The Free Edition covers up to
      100 Test Cases per Conversion: you may perform an Assessment of a
      Conversion of any size, but you may convert the Test Cases of a
      Conversion, and Deploy their Converted Assets, only if it holds 100
      Test Cases or fewer.
   c. Licensed Edition. If you have an Order and Merito has issued you a
      License File, then, subject to the terms of this Agreement and
      payment of the fees in your Order, you may also, under the license
      in section 1.b, convert the Test Cases of any Conversion that your
      License File covers, and Deploy their Converted Assets, within the
      term, the Test Case limit, and the ALM projects that your Order and
      License File state (the "Licensed Edition"). A License File that
      names ALM projects covers only the Test Cases of those projects,
      including when you convert them on a file system.
   d. Assessment Output. Assessment Output is for assessment only. You
      may use it to evaluate, plan, scope, and budget a migration, and
      you may send it to Merito under section 3. Until you may convert
      the Test Cases of its Conversion under section 1.b or 1.c, a test
      the Software builds during an Assessment is an evaluation copy: you
      may open, inspect, and run it to evaluate the Software, but you may
      not Deploy it or otherwise use it instead of converting the Test
      Case it was built from. A Conversion of more than 100 Test Cases
      needs the Licensed Edition, with a License File that covers it,
      before any of its Test Cases are converted or Deployed, including
      from tests built during an Assessment. If Test Cases are converted
      or Deployed without the license this Agreement requires, those
      converted tests are not Converted Assets, and the license in
      section 5 does not extend to the helper code in them. You must then
      stop using those converted tests until you obtain a License File
      that covers their Conversion. Merito may also seek any other remedy
      available at law or in equity, including injunctive relief.
   e. License Files. A License File is issued to you alone. The Software
      checks it on your computer, without contacting Merito. Your License
      File records what your Order grants; if they differ, your Order
      prevails, and Merito will promptly issue a corrected License File.
      Subject to your Order, a License File gives no rights for a
      Conversion it does not cover, or after its expiry date; the Free
      Edition then applies.
   f. Restore and roll back. Whatever your edition, you may use the
      Software to restore tests from the backups it made, to roll back
      tests it converted, and to finish or undo a run that was interrupted
      while converting Test Cases, if converting them was permitted when
      that run started.
   g. The Software's count. The Software counts Test Cases to help you
      stay within a Test Case limit. Its count is a guide only. The
      definitions in section 1.a govern, and the Software allowing you to
      convert or Deploy Test Cases does not mean this Agreement permits
      it. In particular, the Software does not count Test Cases in ALM's
      Unattached area, and it accepts any valid License File on a file
      system, even one limited to named ALM projects. Merito does not
      warrant that the Software's count matches section 1.a. The Software
      may count a test that section 1.a excludes, such as a backup it made
      whose converted test has been moved or deleted; you may delete that
      backup and run the Software again.

2. RESTRICTIONS
   Except as expressly permitted by this Agreement or by applicable law
   that cannot be contractually waived, you shall not, and shall not
   permit any third party to:
   a. copy, distribute, rent, lease, lend, sell, sublicense, or otherwise
      transfer the Software to any third party;
   b. reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Software, except to
      the extent such restriction is prohibited by applicable law;
   c. modify, adapt, or create derivative works of the Software;
   d. remove, alter, or obscure any proprietary notices in the Software or
      its output;
   e. use the Software to provide services to third parties (including as
      a service bureau or managed migration service) without a separate
      written agreement with Merito;
   f. publish, or disclose to any third party, the results of any
      benchmark or evaluation of the Software without Merito's prior
      written consent, except that you may share Assessment Output and
      your own evaluation of the Software with your employees, and with
      your contractors and professional advisers who need it to help you
      evaluate, plan, or carry out a migration of your own test assets and
      who are bound by duties of confidentiality at least as protective as
      this section, and you are responsible for their compliance with this
      Agreement;
   g. divide a Conversion or otherwise work around a Test Case limit.
      Whatever your reason, (i) Test Cases that you copy or move out of an
      ALM project or folder continue to count toward any Conversion of
      that ALM project or folder, and (ii) when you run the Software
      separately on two or more folders that share a parent folder, the
      Test Cases in all of them count as one Conversion of that parent
      folder;
   h. remove, disable, bypass, or interfere with the Software's count of
      Test Cases, its Test Case limit, or its check of License Files,
      including by modifying the Software or its data, running a modified
      copy of it, or changing your computer's date; or
   i. create, alter, or forge a License File, use a License File that
      Merito did not issue to you, use a License File that is limited to
      named ALM projects to convert Test Cases from any other ALM project,
      including on a file system, or share, publish, or transfer a License
      File to anyone else.
   Merito may ask you, no more than once in any twelve (12) month period
   unless Merito has reasonable grounds to believe you have exceeded a
   Test Case limit, to confirm in writing the artifact count of any
   Conversion you have converted and, for a file-system run under a
   License File limited to named ALM projects, the ALM project its Test
   Cases came from. A Conversion's artifact count is the number of its
   Test Cases. You will respond within thirty (30) days with a written
   confirmation signed by someone authorized to bind you, together with
   reasonable supporting records, such as the Software's scoping summary
   for that Conversion. Failing to respond, or giving a materially
   inaccurate count or source, is a breach of this Agreement, and
   section 1.d applies to any Test Cases converted beyond your Test Case
   limit or outside the ALM projects your License File names.

3. CUSTOMER DATA AND ALM ENVIRONMENTS
   a. The Software reads and, when explicitly enabled by you, writes to
      your ALM projects and UFT test assets. You are solely responsible
      for (i) maintaining complete, restorable backups of every ALM
      project and file-system asset the Software touches, and (ii)
      verifying converted assets before relying on them. The Software's
      backup confirmation prompts do not create any Merito obligation to
      preserve or recover your data.
   b. You represent that you hold all rights and consents necessary for
      the Software to access and process the test assets you point it at.
   c. The Software operates entirely within your environment. It connects
      only to the ALM server and UFT One installation you point it at. It
      sends no usage data, test assets, reports, or other information to
      Merito, and it checks License Files without contacting Merito. The
      Software and its reports contain links to Merito's website, which
      open in your web browser only when you click them. Those links carry
      campaign tags that tell Merito the visit came from UFT Phoenix and
      contain no test names, counts, or other data about your tests or
      environment, although following the link shown when a conversion
      exceeds its limit tells Merito that it did. Your visit to Merito's
      website is governed by Merito's Privacy Policy at
      https://www.merito.com/legal-docs/commercial-privacy-policy.pdf and
      Cookie Policy at https://www.merito.com/legal/cookie-policy. Merito
      receives only what you choose to send it, and you have no obligation
      to send Merito anything.
   d. If you choose to send Merito the scoping summary or other output of
      the Software so that Merito can scope or quote a license or services
      for you, Merito will keep it confidential for three (3) years after
      receipt, or for any trade secret for as long as it remains a trade
      secret, use it only for that scoping and quoting, and delete it
      within thirty (30) days after you ask. Merito may keep (i) copies in
      routine backups until they are overwritten in the ordinary course,
      (ii) copies it must keep to comply with law or a legal hold, and
      (iii) the quotes, Orders, and related records it creates, including
      the Test Case counts and other figures in them, and anything Merito
      keeps remains subject to this section 3.d. These obligations do not
      apply to information that is or becomes public through no fault of
      Merito, that Merito already knew or develops independently, or that
      Merito receives from a third party without a duty of
      confidentiality. Merito may disclose it if required by law, after
      giving you prompt notice where the law allows. The scoping summary
      contains no test code; other reports can contain excerpts of your
      tests, so check what you send.

4. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
   a. The Software interoperates with, but does not include, OpenText UFT
      One and OpenText Application Quality Management (formerly ALM/Quality
      Center). You are responsible for holding valid licenses for those
      products.
   b. The offline package includes redistributed third-party components,
      among them a CPython runtime and the libraries it links (including
      OpenSSL, SQLite, zlib-ng, zlib, Expat, mpdecimal, and liblzma), its
      Tcl/Tk libraries, pywin32, typing-extensions, and the Titillium Web
      typeface. Each is licensed under its own terms, which are
      identified, with the location of each license's full text, in the
      THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt file distributed with the Software. Nothing
      in this Agreement limits your rights under those licenses.

5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
   The Software is licensed, not sold. Merito and its licensors retain all
   right, title, and interest in and to the Software, including all
   intellectual property rights. Converted Assets are your property; the
   templates the Software uses to convert tests, the compatibility helper
   code emitted into converted assets, and the Software itself remain
   Merito's property, and Merito grants you a perpetual, royalty-free
   license to use such emitted helper code solely as embedded in, or loaded
   by, your Converted Assets. That license covers both helper code written
   into a Converted Asset and the shared helper library the Software
   installs alongside your assets (PhoenixVBRuntime.pfl), including the
   copies of it the Software places in your ALM project or output folders.
   Tests the Software builds during an Assessment are not Converted Assets.
   Your rights in your own test content are unaffected, and Merito grants
   you a license to use the helper code in those tests solely as section
   1.d allows, for as long as this Agreement remains in effect. Once you
   may convert the Test Cases of a Conversion under section 1.b or 1.c, a
   test built during an Assessment of that Conversion becomes a Converted
   Asset.

6. SUPPORT AND UPDATES
   a. Support and maintenance for the Licensed Edition, if any, are
      provided under your Order.
   b. Merito provides support for the Free Edition on a best-effort basis
      only. Merito will try to help, for example with a diagnostics
      bundle you choose to send, but it does not commit to any response
      time, resolution, or level of service, and it may stop providing
      such support at any time.
   c. If you send Merito a diagnostics bundle or other information for
      support, Merito will keep it confidential for three (3) years after
      receipt, or for any trade secret for as long as it remains a trade
      secret, use it only to provide that support, and delete it within
      thirty (30) days after you ask. Merito may keep (i) copies in
      routine backups until they are overwritten in the ordinary course,
      (ii) copies it must keep to comply with law or a legal hold, and
      (iii) the support records it creates, and anything Merito keeps
      remains subject to this section 6.c. The exceptions and the
      permitted disclosure in section 3.d apply to this section as well.
   d. Updates, whether supplied under support or otherwise, are governed
      by this Agreement as presented when you install them.

7. TERM AND TERMINATION
   a. This Agreement is effective until terminated. It terminates
      automatically if you breach section 2.h or 2.i, and Merito may
      terminate it by notice if you breach any other term. If you breach
      section 1.b, 1.c, 1.d, or 2.g, or the last paragraph of section 2,
      this Agreement terminates only if you do not cure the breach, as
      section 1.d allows, within thirty (30) days after Merito's notice of
      it. Upon termination you must cease all use of the Software, except
      that for up to thirty (30) days you may use it to restore tests from
      the backups it made or to roll back tests it converted, and you must
      then destroy all copies. Sections 1.d, 2 (except section 2.f, which
      survives for two (2) years after termination), and 3 through 10
      survive termination.
   b. Merito may change or end the Free Edition at any time. A change,
      such as a different Test Case limit, applies to a version of the
      Software once you accept this Agreement on installing that version.
      Merito may end the Free Edition for all versions by notice to you,
      including by email to the address used to request the Software, and
      by posting the notice on its website, in each case at least thirty
      (30) days before the end takes effect; after that date, you may use
      the Software only under the Licensed Edition, except as section 1.f
      allows.
   c. Your Licensed Edition rights last for the term your Order states.
      When a License File expires, the Free Edition applies until Merito
      issues you a new one.
   d. Ending the Free Edition, a License File, an Order, or this
      Agreement does not affect Converted Assets you produced before
      then, or the license in section 5 to the helper code in them.

